    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nwhen we use `:lua vim.diagnostic.goto_next()` to show the details of next diagnostic which is far from the cursor,  we have possibility to miss the show of it.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nnightly\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. run `:lua vim.diagnostic.goto_next()` move to a diagnostic in a distance\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nmove cursor then show details of diagnostic \n\n### Actual behavior\n\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/62557596/c9338826-0b3e-40f3-bc93-29123a841f50",
